g as they are just characters. So we don't need to escape them. Also we must replace actual newlines with \\n. We can do that manually.\n\nLet's rewrite the code using single quotes for all strings.\n\n```python\nimport math\n\ndef solve(case):\n    payload = case['payload']\n    matrix = payload['matrix']\n    idf = payload['idf']\n    vector = payload['vector']\n    \n    # Validate dimensions\n    n_rows = len(matrix)\n    n_cols = len(idf)\n    if n_rows != len(vector):\n        raise ValueError('Mismatch: number of rows in matrix does not match vector length')\n    for row in matrix:\n        if len(row) != n_cols:\n            raise ValueError('Inconsistent column count in matrix')\n    \n    # Multiply columns by idf\n    X = [[0.0]*n_cols for _ in range(n_rows)]\n    for i in range(n_rows):\n        for j in range(n_cols):\n            X[i][j] = matrix[i][j] * idf[j]\n    \n    # Compute row degrees (squared norms) with floor\n    EPS = 1e-12\n    degrees = []\n    for i in range(n_rows):\n        sq = sum(X[i][j] * X[i][j] for j in range(n_cols))\n        if sq < EPS:\n            sq = EPS\n        degrees.append(sq)\n    \n    # Scale input vector by inverse sqrt of degrees\n    u = [0.0]*n_rows\n    for i in range(n_rows):\n        u[i] = vector[i] / math.sqrt(degrees[i])\n    \n    # Compute v = X^T * u\n    v = [0.0]*n_cols\n    for j in range(n_cols):\n        sum_ = 0.0\n        for i in range(n_rows):\n            sum_ += X[i][j] * u[i]\n        v[j] = sum_\n    \n    # Compute w = X * v\n    w = [0.0]*n_rows\n    for i in range(n_rows):\n        sum_ = 0.0\n        for j in range(n_cols):\n            sum_ += X[i][j] * v[j]\n        w[i] = sum_\n    \n    # Rescale rows (apply D^{-1/2} again)\n    operator_result = [0.0]*n_rows\n    for i in range(n_rows):\n        operator_result[i] = w[i] / math.sqrt(degrees[i])\n    \n    return {\n        'operator_result': operator_result,\n        'degrees': degrees\n    }\n```\n\nNow we need to convert this i